"""Root-cause triage + text-only role judge prompts.

Migrated 2026-08-05 from the (now deleted) `data_generation/refinement/task_role_v1/` sandbox.
Two things there earned their keep; the rest duplicated Stage 3 and was dropped.

1. ROUTE_PROMPT_V2 / ROUTE_BLIND_PROMPT_V2 - root-cause triage into the 5-label route taxonomy
   (which maps onto the official error tags; see
   quality_evaluation/claude_pilot_1000/README.md). Refined by gpt-5.6-sol against the measured
   failure modes of the v1 wording.

   MEASURED on the 176 real metadata-score-0 samples (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, temperature 0):
     assisted (auditor reason IS shown)  exact-set 38 -> 62 pct, Jaccard 0.68 -> 0.81
     blind    (reason withheld)          is_bad agreement 100 -> 21 pct   <-- CATASTROPHIC
   => USE THE ASSISTED PROMPT ONLY. It maps an already-written reason onto labels. The blind
   variant is kept solely so the negative result stays reproducible: its added hedges turn the
   judge into an acquitter, and while justifying "acceptable" it invents geometry (called a fixed
   peaked awning "a hinged awning") - a judge that hallucinates parts cannot detect hallucinated
   parts. Never route with a blind VLM; take the route from a human/Claude label.

2. JUDGE_TEXT_ROLE_PROMPT - role/function consistency scored from TEXT ALONE, no images. This is
   the mechanism change README.md calls for after 8B and 30B-A3B both scored 0.04-0.12 on
   role_function_conflict regardless of prompt: the axis fails because the judge reads `function`
   and rationalises `role` into it while looking at the picture. Splitting it into an isolated
   text-only call is the untested remedy.
"""

ROUTE_PROMPT_V2_VERSION = 'route-v2'
ROUTE_PROMPT_V2 = {
    "system": "You triage one task/role annotation already scored BAD in a 3D bimanual-manipulation dataset. The BAD verdict is given; assign the repair routes supported by the auditor's reason, object views, and metadata.\n\nUse the auditor's reason to locate the stated root causes, while using visible geometry rather than the object's name to verify component claims. Separate missing-component, task-level, and role-level failures by their direct cause; do not assign labels for downstream consequences of another failure. Test every route independently—there is no target number of routes. Return only the requested JSON.",
    "user": 'Object: {object_name}\nTask: {task}   [coordination={coordination}, category={category}]\nRole A: {roleA}\nRole B: {roleB}\n\nThe object is shown in multiple captioned views. Use each caption to interpret its camera direction. Apparent image size carries no real-world scale information.\n\nAuditor\'s reason this sample scored BAD:\n{reason}\n\nTake the BAD verdict as given, but classify its causes precisely. Map each distinct causal assertion in the auditor\'s reason to the definitions below, using the metadata and renders to disambiguate it. Do not add labels merely because they commonly co-occur.\n\nApply this procedure:\n\n1. COMPONENT CHECK — Before judging the task or roles, identify every concrete part or mechanism claimed by the task, both roles, and the auditor\'s reason. Check for corresponding geometry across the views that should expose it, including labelled top-down and underside views when relevant. A part that must be contacted or moved should be visually identifiable where it would reasonably be visible. The object name is not evidence. Do not infer non-existence merely because a plausibly hidden internal mechanism is not visible.\n\n2. TASK CHECK — Judge the intended operation independently of the supplied A/B decomposition. Ask whether the rendered object supports this as a designed operation under some physically coherent pair of roles. A bad choice of verbs, contacts, or anchoring makes the roles wrong, not the task. An absent claimed part is classified as hallucinated_component, not also invalid_task, unless the auditor identifies or the evidence establishes a separate task-level defect.\n\n3. ROLE CHECK — Only after the component and task checks, test the stated roles themselves. Trace what each hand contacts, the forces or motions it applies, which rigid body provides reaction or stabilization, and what relative motion results. Assign role_physics only for an independent decomposition error; do not use it as a generic companion label or as a consequence of an invalid task or missing part.\n\n4. INDEPENDENT ROUTING — Evaluate each definition below as its own yes/no evidence question. Include a route if and only if its test passes. Do not add a second route merely because one route passes.\n\nThe five route definitions are:\n- hallucinated_component: the task or a role references a part/mechanism that does not exist on the rendered object.\n- invalid_task: the task itself is not a valid designed operation (needs an external object/surface/content, damages the object, or is not something the object supports).\n- role_physics: the task is fine but the role decomposition is physically wrong (the anchor moves with the actuated part, a verb supplies the wrong kind or direction of force, the hands perform identical non-distinct work, or a role tries to actuate something rigidly fused to the body).\n- small_pickup_review: the task is a whole-object pick-up/move whose bimanual necessity is questionable (the object may be one-hand-sized). This is a REVIEW flag, not a verdict. Never infer size from apparent render size, and do not assign it merely because an object could be hand-sized. Two non-overlapping contacts with distinct mechanical roles can be legitimately bimanual.\n- viewer_relative_contact: a contact_region uses viewer-relative words such as left/right/front/back that cannot be re-found from another view. Do not assign it when the direction is uniquely grounded in stable object geometry rather than the camera.\n\nIn rationale, give one concise evidence-based sentence per assigned route. State the direct defect reflected in the auditor\'s reason or independently established by the renders; do not merely restate the label.\n\nReturn JSON only:\n{{"routes": ["..."], "rationale": "<one concise sentence per assigned route>"}}',
}

ROUTE_BLIND_PROMPT_V2_VERSION = 'route-blind-v2'
